## 3. Batch Operations

### ⛔ ANTI-PATTERN: Row-by-Row Insert (N+1 Pattern)

```java
// ❌ WRONG — N round trips, ~50% time spent in network idle
for (Order order : orders) {
    stmt.executeUpdate("INSERT INTO orders VALUES (...)");
}
```

### ✅ Correct: Use Batching

```java
// ✅ CORRECT — single round trip, 10-100× faster
PreparedStatement ps = conn.prepareStatement(
    "INSERT INTO orders (id, customer_id, amount) VALUES (?, ?, ?)");
for (Order order : orders) {
    ps.setObject(1, order.id());
    ps.setObject(2, order.customerId());
    ps.setBigDecimal(3, order.amount());
    ps.addBatch();
}
ps.executeBatch();
```

- Batch 128–256 rows per `executeBatch()` call
- For very large loads, use `IMPORT INTO` or `COPY FROM`
- In Python, use `executemany()` or `psycopg2.extras.execute_values()`
- In Go, use `pgx.Batch` or multi-row `INSERT INTO ... VALUES (...), (...), ...`

