## 11. Prepared Statement Best Practices

- **Always use parameterized queries** — prevents SQL injection, enables plan caching
- **Always list explicit columns** — never `SELECT *` (cached plans break on schema changes)
- **Close statements when done** — prevents resource leaks on CockroachDB nodes

```go
// ✅ CORRECT — parameterized, explicit columns
rows, err := db.QueryContext(ctx,
    "SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE tenant_id = $1 AND active = true",
    tenantID)
```

---

## 12. Error Handling Summary

| Error Type | SQLSTATE | Retry? | Action |
|-----------|----------|--------|--------|
| Serialization failure | `40001` | ✅ Yes | Retry entire transaction with backoff |
| Connection errors | `08xxx` | ✅ Yes | Retry with new connection |
| Admin shutdown | `57P01` | ✅ Yes | Retry with backoff (node draining) |
| Duplicate key | `23505` | ❌ No | Application logic error — fix the INSERT |
| Foreign key violation | `23503` | ❌ No | Referenced row doesn't exist — fix data |
| Check constraint | `23514` | ❌ No | Data doesn't meet constraint — fix data |
| Syntax error | `42601` | ❌ No | Fix the SQL |
| Undefined table | `42P01` | ❌ No | Table doesn't exist — check schema |
| Transaction too large | N/A | ❌ No | Chunk into smaller transactions |

