## 13. Consolidated Bad SQL & Application Patterns

| # | Bad Pattern | Why It's Bad | Fix |
|---|------------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | SAVEPOINT + ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT as retry | 40001 aborts entire txn, not fixable | Full-transaction retry loop |
| 2 | Read-modify-write on hot rows without retry | 40001 errors, lost updates | Use RetryableExecutor or crdb.ExecuteTx |
| 3 | SELECT large JSON + UPDATE in same txn | Long txn, idle time, contention | Read-write split with AS OF SYSTEM TIME |
| 4 | Row-by-row INSERT in a loop (N+1) | N round trips, ~50% idle time | addBatch/executeBatch |
| 5 | SELECT * without WHERE or LIMIT | Full table scan, blocks other txns | Always use WHERE + LIMIT |
| 6 | UPDATE without WHERE clause | Bulk write, exceeds row limits | Add WHERE, set session guardrails |
| 7 | 20+ statements in one txn (KB each) | Accumulates toward 16MB limit | Commit every 5–10 statements |
| 8 | Storing multi-MB blobs inline | Slow Raft, range split backpressure | Object storage (S3/GCS) + DB reference |
| 9 | SERIAL/SEQUENCE primary keys | Write hotspot, one node CPU spike | UUID with gen_random_uuid() |
| 10 | Multiple DDL in BEGIN/COMMIT | Not atomic, partial commit risk | One DDL per implicit transaction |
| 11 | SELECT * in prepared statements | Schema change breaks cached plan | Explicit column lists |
| 12 | No retry logic for 40001 | Silent data loss, failed transactions | Mandatory retry wrapper |
| 13 | Fixed-delay retries (no jitter) | Thundering herd on retry | Exponential backoff with random jitter |
| 14 | Retrying non-retryable errors | Wasted resources, infinite loops | Check SQLSTATE before retrying |
| 15 | Using PostgreSQL ORM backend | Missing retry support, DDL issues | Use CockroachDB-specific adapter |
| 16 | More threads on hot rows | Lower TPS, more 40001 waste | Redesign schema to avoid hot rows |
| 17 | sslmode=disable in production | No encryption, MITM vulnerable | Always sslmode=verify-full |
| 18 | No connection pool validation | Stale connections after node drain | Set connectionTestQuery + keepalive |
| 19 | Mixing DDL with DML in transactions | Deadlocks, partial schema changes | Separate DDL from DML completely |
| 20 | No session guardrails in dev/test | Runaway queries hit production | Set transaction_rows_read/written_err |

---

## 14. General Rules (Quick Reference)

1. **Keep transactions SHORT** — <10 statements, <4MB total payload
2. **Keep rows SMALL** — <1MB per row; use chunking or object storage for large data
3. **Use UUID primary keys** — `gen_random_uuid()`, never SERIAL
4. **Transaction retry is MANDATORY** — wrap every write transaction in a retry loop
5. **Use exponential backoff with jitter** — not fixed delays
6. **Use `AS OF SYSTEM TIME`** for read-heavy operations outside write transactions
7. **Use batching** — `addBatch`/`executeBatch` instead of row-by-row loops
8. **One DDL per implicit transaction** — no BEGIN/COMMIT wrapping
9. **Always list explicit columns** — no `SELECT *` in prepared statements or application code
10. **Set session guardrails** in dev/test — `transaction_rows_read_err`, `transaction_rows_written_err`
11. **Use CockroachDB ORM adapters** — not raw PostgreSQL backends
12. **Always `sslmode=verify-full`** in production
13. **Set `autocommit_before_ddl = on`** when using ORM migration tools
14. **Monitor** — `SHOW JOBS` for schema changes, DB Console for contention
